Subject: [PATCH 069/168] =?UTF-8?q?fix(desktop):=20wenshu=20app=20icon=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20remove=20white=20background,=20restore=20macOS=20ro?=
 =?UTF-8?q?unded-corner=20mask?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Icon had a 863x863 white background filling 95% of canvas, leaving only 80px transparent margin. macOS Icon Services couldn't apply the rounded-rect mask (no alpha to mask against), so the icon rendered as a square white tile filling its tile.

Fix:
- Strip the white background; keep calligraphy on transparent canvas
- Resize calligraphy to fit 720px max(dim) on 1024 canvas — gives ~150px safe-zone margin on each side
- Rebuild icon.icns from masked PNG (10 sizes: 16/32/64/128/256/512/1024 + @2x), all RGBA
- Regenerate apple-touch-icon.png at 180x180 from the new transparent source
- Rebuild .app; icon in /Applications/文枢.app/Contents/Resources/icon.icns updated

Verified 3 locations after rebuild:
- Dock: rounded corners, normal tile size, calligraphy on transparent
- Activity Monitor: 文枢 Helper process shows same calligraphy icon
- Finder /Applications: rounded corners, no white background, matches Hermes/Feishu

Touched:
- apps/desktop/assets/icon.png (1024x1024 RGBA, 242KB)
- apps/desktop/assets/icon.icns (10-size iconset, 492KB)
- apps/desktop/public/apple-touch-icon.png (180x180, 12KB)

Out of scope (not committed): brand-mark.tsx (changed in prior attempt, not icon related)
---
 apps/desktop/assets/icon.icns            | Bin 370411 -> 492289 bytes
 apps/desktop/assets/icon.png             | Bin 258920 -> 242348 bytes
 apps/desktop/public/apple-touch-icon.png | Bin 13168 -> 11673 bytes
 3 files changed, 0 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)

